dim][/dim] · [bold #D7AFFF][/dim]3[dim][/bold #D7AFFF] waves[/dim]\n[dim]   Path: [#87AFFF][/dim]plans:202608/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]artifacts_tab_icons.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim] Prompt: [#87AFFF][/dim]prompts/202608/artifacts_tab_icons.md[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Bead: [#87AFFF][/dim]sase-kv[/#87AFFF]\n[dim]   Page: [#87AFFF][/dim]https://github.com/sase-org/sase--beads/blob/main/pages/sase-kv/[bold #87AFFF][/#87AFFF]README.md[/bold #87AFFF]\n[dim]  1 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Required `ref.icon` in the artifact ref provider spec wire[/bold #D7AFFF]    [bold black on #87D7FF] small  [/bold black on #87D7FF]\n    [#AF87FF]wire[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]wire: add a required `icon` string to the Rust [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]`ArtifactRefProviderRefSpecWire`, validate it as a bounded [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]one-or-two-cell glyph, and cover accept/reject and digest cases in the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]Rust unit tests.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  2 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Icons, cell-accurate click ranges, and reflow-to-fit in [/bold #D7AFFF]      [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n      [bold #D7AFFF]PanelTabStrip[/bold #D7AFFF]\n    [#AF87FF]strip[dim] · [dim][/dim]no dependencies[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]strip: give `PanelTab` an icon, render it between the number and the [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]label, measure click ranges in terminal cells instead of characters, and[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]add an opt-in reflow ladder that keeps every tab visible and clickable [/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF]when the strip cannot fit its full render.[/#D7D7AF]\n    [#D7D7AF][/#D7D7AF]\n[dim]  3 [bold #AF87FF][/dim]◆ [bold #D7AFFF][/bold #AF87FF]Icons on Artifacts tab descriptors and in sidecar ref config[/bold #D7AFFF]  [bold black on #FFD75F] medium [/bold black on #FFD75F]\n    [#AF87FF]tabs[dim] · [dim][/dim]after wire[/#AF87FF][/dim]\n    [#D7D7AF]tabs: add a b